<title>USA: Paccar cites soft demand, cuts Q4 build.</title>
<headline>Paccar cites soft demand, cuts Q4 build.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Wash. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>PACCAR Inc on Monday attributed lower third quarter results to continued soft demand for trucks in the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>In response, the heavy-duty truck maker said it has further reduced U.S. truck build rates at the beginning of the fourth quarter.&quot;</p>
<p>Earlier in the day, the company reported that third quarter earnings were $1.31 per share, compared to $1.76 a year-ago. Sales for the quarter were $1.0 billion compared to $1.1 billion a year-ago.</p>
</text>
